WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.710 --> 00:00:05.540
Game of Thrones Season 6 Episode 5 is out,
and it is huge, so let’s begin.

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:09.400
At Mole’s Town – a little village just
south of the Wall – Sansa confronts Littlefinger

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.650
for having given her to Ramsay.

00:00:11.650 --> 00:00:15.769
Littlefinger says he’s sorry, he didn’t
know Ramsay was so cruel, and apparently he’s

00:00:15.769 --> 00:00:20.669
telling the truth, he really didn’t know
– which is a pretty major fuck-up, right?

00:00:20.669 --> 00:00:24.789
He gave up Sansa, one of his most valuable
strategic assets, and someone he loves in

00:00:24.789 --> 00:00:29.859
his own creepy way, to a family that’s famous
for flaying and betraying Starks , somehow

00:00:29.859 --> 00:00:32.500
not suspecting that they’d hurt her.

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:36.860
Littlefinger is usually a master manipulator
but with Ramsay he made a mistake, and he

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:42.690
admits it – he presents himself to Sansa
unprotected, at her mercy, to apologise.

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:47.420
So as much as Littlefinger is using Sansa
for his own political goals , he also seems

00:00:47.420 --> 00:00:50.000
to sincerely want Sansa to forgive him.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.859
He’s a complicated character.

00:00:51.859 --> 00:00:55.909
Like, this meeting happens at Mole’s Town,
right, which is interesting because Mole’s

00:00:55.909 --> 00:00:59.379
Town has the brothel where the men of the
Night’s Watch come – at least until the

00:00:59.379 --> 00:01:01.559
wildlings sack the town in Season 4.

00:01:01.559 --> 00:01:06.350
But it’s in the ruins of that brothel that
Littlefinger chooses to meet Sansa – just

00:01:06.350 --> 00:01:11.380
as he meets Cat in a brothel, and Olenna in
a brothel – prostitution is a big theme

00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:15.390
in Littlefinger’s story, in fact the whole
situation of Petyr giving Sansa to Ramsay

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:18.090
kind of is an act of pimpery, right?

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:22.420
So much of Littlefinger’s character is rooted
in his sexual history with Lysa and Catelyn,

00:01:22.420 --> 00:01:27.090
which is tied up with his feelings of self-worth
and power and status – “I’m not going

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:28.090
to fight them.

00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:29.370
I’m going to fuck them.

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:30.460
That’s what I know.

00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:36.079
That’s what I am” – in Littlefinger’s
mind, sex is deeply linked to power and control,

00:01:36.079 --> 00:01:41.180
so it’s no coincidence that prostitution
and pimpery are recurring themes in his story.

00:01:41.180 --> 00:01:45.630
Anyway, Littlefinger offers Sansa the support
of his knights from the Vale, but she refuses

00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:46.630
him.

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:47.939
She’s probably right not to trust him.

00:01:47.939 --> 00:01:49.670
But at the same time, she and Jon and co.

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:52.270
really do need more men right now.

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:55.700
Those knights will probably end up in battle
at Winterfell anyway, cause you don’t bring

00:01:55.700 --> 00:01:57.590
an army to the north and not use it.

00:01:57.590 --> 00:02:01.700
Also, Littlefinger says the Tullys, led by
Brynden “Blackfish” Tully, have retaken

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:05.750
Riverrun, and may be able to support Sansa
in the north, which could be a huge help.

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:10.431
And on his way out, Littlefinger calls Jon
Sansa’s half-brother, not brother, which

00:02:10.431 --> 00:02:13.890
seems to make Sansa doubt if she can trust
Jon.

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:17.610
In Braavos, Arya trains with “the waif”,
because hitting people with sticks is clearly

00:02:17.610 --> 00:02:22.050
the path to becoming a great assassin, then
Jaqen turns up and tells Arya the story of

00:02:22.050 --> 00:02:24.620
how the Faceless Men began.

00:02:24.620 --> 00:02:29.000
This was hundreds of years ago in Valyria,
the empire of the original “dragonlords”,

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:33.840
who ruled most of the known world through
the power of their dragons and their slaves.

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:37.980
In the books, we’re told the slaves would
mine for gold beneath volcanic mountains called

00:02:37.980 --> 00:02:42.260
the Fourteen Flames, and that the mines were
so hot and the work so hard that slaves would

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:46.620
pray for “an end to [their] pain” – so
the first Faceless Man was someone who killed

00:02:46.620 --> 00:02:51.240
the slaves who suffered the most . Arya says
he should have killed the slave masters, not

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:56.260
the slaves, and she’s told that “He would
bring the gift to them as well” . Some fans

00:02:56.260 --> 00:03:01.650
believe this means that the Faceless Men caused
the Doom of Valyria, the massive fiery catastrophe

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:04.840
that suddenly destroyed the empire two hundred
years ago.

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:08.780
If it’s true that the Faceless Men were
behind the downfall of the original dragonlords,

00:03:08.780 --> 00:03:13.900
they might not be a fan of Daenerys, this
new Valyrian queen , conquering cities with

00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:15.400
her dragons.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:19.030
Maybe the Faceless Men will try to kill Dany.

00:03:19.030 --> 00:03:22.760
Arya’s told to kill an actress, so she goes
to see a play.

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:26.540
The play is a retelling of recent events in
King’s Landing – the death of King Robert,

00:03:26.540 --> 00:03:29.210
the downfall of Ned, the marriage of Sansa
to Tyrion.

00:03:29.210 --> 00:03:33.420
It’s cool to see how the public perception
of what happened is so wrong – like, Ned’s

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:37.340
portrayed as an idiot who wanted the Throne,
when he was the opposite.

00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:40.930
Tyrion plots with then betrays Ned, when that
was actually Littlefinger.

00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:43.750
Cersei tries to follow the rules, when she
actually broke them.

00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:47.910
Joffrey’s a noble prince instead of a nasty
little shit, and he’s kind to Sansa when

00:03:47.910 --> 00:03:50.170
he actually threatened and beat her.

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:54.220
And Tyrion wants to marry and sleep with Sansa,
when in truth he wanted neither.

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:58.280
But the real drama of this scene is that Arya
has to relive the horrors that happened to

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:02.890
her family, she’s forced to watch her father’s
execution for the second time.

00:04:02.890 --> 00:04:07.120
Maybe the Faceless Men are testing her here
by confronting her with memories of her family

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:11.230
– to become “no one”, she’d have to
let go of the people she loves.

00:04:11.230 --> 00:04:15.890
Afterwards, Arya spies on Lady Crane, the
woman she’s meant to murder, and she seems

00:04:15.890 --> 00:04:20.139
nice, so back at the House, Arya talks as
though she doesn’t wanna kill Crane.

00:04:20.139 --> 00:04:23.509
Jaqen says she she’s not meant to care if
she’s nice, she’s not meant to ask questions,

00:04:23.509 --> 00:04:27.840
she’s meant to blindly serve the Many-Faced
God, the god of death.

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:29.800
So again, Arya’s being tested.

00:04:29.800 --> 00:04:32.669
Will she give up her sense of justice and
murder an innocent woman?

00:04:32.669 --> 00:04:37.250
Jaqen says she’s on her last chance, it’s
make or break time, and hints from the books

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:43.080
and show suggest she’s gonna leave the Faceless
Men – and it’s gonna be bloody.

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:47.719
Beyond the Wall, Bran has a vision of the
children of the forest creating the white

00:04:47.719 --> 00:04:48.939
walkers.

00:04:48.939 --> 00:04:53.090
This would have happened some ten thousand
years ago, when humans first came to Westeros

00:04:53.090 --> 00:04:57.900
and started a war with the children, who had
been there long before . Eventually the children

00:04:57.900 --> 00:05:02.060
and the First Men made peace, in an agreement
called the Pact, but this scene seems to suggest

00:05:02.060 --> 00:05:06.409
that sometime before the Pact, the children
created white walkers as a weapon for their

00:05:06.409 --> 00:05:08.249
war against the humans.

00:05:08.249 --> 00:05:11.430
At some point the children must have lost
control of the walkers, because thousands

00:05:11.430 --> 00:05:16.050
of years later, the Long Night happened, when
white walkers attacked and almost took over

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:20.469
Westeros . They were stopped by the humans
and the children working together to fight

00:05:20.469 --> 00:05:24.930
and win the War for the Dawn – after the
War, the Wall was built to keep the walkers

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:28.520
out – though they didn’t make the walkers
pay for the Wall . This was all thousands

00:05:28.520 --> 00:05:32.100
and thousands of years before the story of
the series begins, so the history’s pretty

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:37.490
hazy here, but we do finally know what walkers
are – they’re like a Frankenstein’s

00:05:37.490 --> 00:05:42.319
monster, an experiment that got loose, or
like, the robots in Terminator, weapons that

00:05:42.319 --> 00:05:43.370
turned on their creators.

00:05:43.370 --> 00:05:46.939
We don’t know how the walkers got out of
the childrens’ control – but maybe the

00:05:46.939 --> 00:05:50.810
problem was that they learned how to make
more of themselves by converting human babies

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:54.770
– it’s a problem when your killing machines
can self-replicate, right?

00:05:54.770 --> 00:05:59.550
Or maybe the problem was the wights, the zombies
that the walkers raise from the dead.

00:05:59.550 --> 00:06:04.560
Cause the thing is, we saw that dragonglass
was used in the creation of the walkers.

00:06:04.560 --> 00:06:08.759
Dragonglass kills walkers, and the children
had lots of dragonglass, so maybe they figured

00:06:08.759 --> 00:06:10.900
they could control the walkers that way.

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:15.729
But the wights, these zombies, aren’t hurt
by dragonglass – the children can’t easily

00:06:15.729 --> 00:06:20.070
stop them – so maybe the walkers went rogue
when they started raising armies of the dead.

00:06:20.070 --> 00:06:25.110
Also, this first white walker appears to be
the Night King, the walker who now leads the

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:26.710
army of the dead.

00:06:26.710 --> 00:06:31.810
Which means the Night King must be like ten
thousand years old – so are the walkers

00:06:31.810 --> 00:06:32.940
immortal?

00:06:32.940 --> 00:06:36.560
That might explain why there have been thousands
of years in between their attacks – they

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:38.940
can afford to be patient.

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:43.560
Also this child of the forest is Leaf, the
same child who’s alive in the present – so

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:45.860
maybe the children are also immortal?

00:06:45.860 --> 00:06:51.639
Weird though, cause in the books, Leaf says
she’s only two hundred years old . Anyway,

00:06:51.639 --> 00:06:55.319
the pattern of stones around the tree where
the walkers are made is similar to the pattern

00:06:55.319 --> 00:07:00.380
of corpses the walkers leave in Season 3 – so
it looks like the walkers mimic the symbols

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:05.110
used by their creators – except the walkers
make them out of corpses.

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:09.680
It really does seem that the walkers are purely
evil, a weapon gone rogue that needs to be

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:10.680
wiped out.

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:12.569
But is it really that simple?

00:07:12.569 --> 00:07:16.770
We know, at least in the books, that they
have language, and culture – maybe they

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:20.949
have a society – cities, or civilisation
in the far north.

00:07:20.949 --> 00:07:25.259
They do do a lot of killing, but they’re
still thinking feeling creatures.

00:07:25.259 --> 00:07:29.800
Look at the Unsullied – they are slaves
raised as soldiers, bred for war – but the

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:33.689
character of Grey Worm shows us that even
people who are created to be mindless killers

00:07:33.689 --> 00:07:37.039
can come to love and live like anyone else.

00:07:37.039 --> 00:07:40.900
It is true that every walker we’ve seen
so far has been a merciless murderer, but

00:07:40.900 --> 00:07:43.749
we can’t assume that every walker’s like
that.

00:07:43.749 --> 00:07:44.749
That’s racist.

00:07:44.749 --> 00:07:48.749
Admittedly it doesn’t look likely that the
walkers will be more than monsters, at least

00:07:48.749 --> 00:07:53.020
in the show, but maybe let’s just think
about the possibility of peace.

00:07:53.020 --> 00:07:57.960
Finally, readers may wonder whether this revelation
about the walkers is true for the books as

00:07:57.960 --> 00:08:03.080
well as the show – because the walkers,
or Others, are very different in the books.

00:08:03.080 --> 00:08:06.930
But as Reddit user Lucifer_Lightbringer points
out, there are strong hints in the books that

00:08:06.930 --> 00:08:10.970
the children made the walkers, for example
one character compares a walker to “some

00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:14.990
child’s snow knight” – which is exactly
what the walkers are if they’re warriors

00:08:14.990 --> 00:08:16.449
for the children.

00:08:16.449 --> 00:08:20.449
So yeah it’s not certain, but it does seem
likely that this stuff is true for the books

00:08:20.449 --> 00:08:21.990
as well as the show.

00:08:21.990 --> 00:08:26.629
At the Iron Islands, the ironborn hold a kingsmoot
to elect their new king.

00:08:26.629 --> 00:08:30.389
Yara talks about making the Iron Islands great
again, building the largest fleet the world’s

00:08:30.389 --> 00:08:35.080
ever seen, and when a man questions her for
being a woman, Theon speaks up in her support.

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:38.270
So everyone seems on side, until Euron arrives.

00:08:38.270 --> 00:08:43.120
He makes fun of Yara and Theon, boldly admits
to killing his brother King Balon, and says

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:46.820
he’ll sail to Daenerys and ally with her
to take Westeros.

00:08:46.820 --> 00:08:50.310
And the people are convinced – they make
Euron their new king.

00:08:50.310 --> 00:08:52.270
This scene is better in the books.

00:08:52.270 --> 00:08:57.470
For starters, Euron has more personality,
he’s this charismatic, swaggering, crazy

00:08:57.470 --> 00:09:02.620
scary pirate, like some darkest-timeline version
of Captain Jack Sparrow.

00:09:02.620 --> 00:09:06.430
He rocks up with this an entourage of bastards
and “mutes and mongrels”, from all over

00:09:06.430 --> 00:09:10.340
the world, he gives out chests of gold to
the ironborn to show how awesome he is , and

00:09:10.340 --> 00:09:15.020
he has a magic horn called Dragonbinder, said
to be able to control dragons.

00:09:15.020 --> 00:09:19.440
He’s got power, he’s got loot, and he’s
got a clear plan, and that’s why the ironborn

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:20.560
choose him.

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:24.830
Yara, or Asha, is also different in the books,
she’s got this great funny speech using

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:29.530
chests of pinecones and turnips and stuff,
she argues for peace, instead this vague marking

00:09:29.530 --> 00:09:35.090
our mark stuff . The show's version's okay,
but the book version's cooler.

00:09:35.090 --> 00:09:40.300
Anyway Aeron Greyjoy, a priest of the Drowned
God, performs a drowning ritual on Euron.

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:44.930
And Euron finds out that Theon and Asha have
run off with their best ships, so Euron says

00:09:44.930 --> 00:09:48.900
he’ll hunt them down and orders the ironborn
to build a thousand ships, as though that’s

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:50.840
something you can do in a short time.

00:09:50.840 --> 00:09:55.190
So it looks like the ironborn are racing to
reach Daenerys, to forge a great alliance

00:09:55.190 --> 00:10:00.690
between the kraken and the dragon – so “let
all the world beware” .

00:10:00.690 --> 00:10:04.080
In Vaes Dothrak, Daenerys and Jorah have a
tearful reunion.

00:10:04.080 --> 00:10:08.620
Jorah shows Dany his greyscale, the stony
disease that’s killing him, and she sends

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:10.470
him off to find a cure.

00:10:10.470 --> 00:10:12.680
In the books, there’s no mention of a cure.

00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:16.850
You can sometimes survive the disease as a
child, like Shireen did, but there’s no

00:10:16.850 --> 00:10:19.340
magic potion that’ll fix it.

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:22.820
In the show, though, there’s a scene where
Stannis says Shireen’s greyscale didn’t

00:10:22.820 --> 00:10:27.250
just go away naturally, he had it cured by
a bunch of maesters and healers.

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:29.700
So maybe Jorah can do something like that.

00:10:29.700 --> 00:10:33.070
Another idea that’s popular at the moment
, is that Jorah might do what the character

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:38.150
Victarion does in the books – he has his
wounded arm healed by a red priest, which

00:10:38.150 --> 00:10:42.100
leaves it all bloody and burned and smoking.

00:10:42.100 --> 00:10:44.440
Maybe Jorah will do something similar.

00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:48.700
Anyway while Jorah the Explorer looks for
a cure, Dany rides for Meereen with her massive

00:10:48.700 --> 00:10:50.130
khalasar.

00:10:50.130 --> 00:10:53.440
In Meereen, Varys says the peace deal with
the masters seems to be working.

00:10:53.440 --> 00:10:57.170
But Tyrion still reckons they have a bit of
PR problem so they go and have a chat with

00:10:57.170 --> 00:11:00.500
Kinvara, the high red priestess of Volantis.

00:11:00.500 --> 00:11:04.120
Kinvara agrees to go “spread the word”
in support of Daenerys, because she believes

00:11:04.120 --> 00:11:08.340
that Dany’s Azor Ahai, or the prince that
was promised – the prophesied saviour of

00:11:08.340 --> 00:11:09.410
the world.

00:11:09.410 --> 00:11:13.810
As Varys points out, Melisandre said the same
thing about Stannis, and now Jon – so the

00:11:13.810 --> 00:11:17.140
red priests really can’t seem to decide
who their chosen one is.

00:11:17.140 --> 00:11:21.510
But Kinvara hits right back at Varys, talking
about his castration by a sorcerer when he

00:11:21.510 --> 00:11:22.520
was a child.

00:11:22.520 --> 00:11:27.370
Varys’ cock and balls were burned in some
magic flame and he remembers hearing words

00:11:27.370 --> 00:11:28.980
coming from the fire.

00:11:28.980 --> 00:11:36.050
Kinvara claims to know what those words were,
and Varys, perhaps understandably, is really

00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:37.050
shaken.

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:42.491
Varys is normally so cool and collected, a
master of disguising his true feelings, but

00:11:42.491 --> 00:11:46.160
here we see him openly uncertain and vulnerable.

00:11:46.160 --> 00:11:49.280
Just like how we saw Littlefinger vulnerable
and exposed.

00:11:49.280 --> 00:11:52.120
Power structures really are shifting this
season.

00:11:52.120 --> 00:11:56.350
Anyway, it does seem good for Dany’s cause
that Kinvara is on side, though Tyrion is

00:11:56.350 --> 00:12:00.560
concerned that she’s wants to burning heretic
and stuff?

00:12:00.560 --> 00:12:06.360
This could be a problem, especially given
that Daenerys is also in a pretty burny mood.

00:12:06.360 --> 00:12:10.900
When they meet, the dragon queen and the red
priestess might get along like a– house

00:12:10.900 --> 00:12:12.200
on fire.

00:12:12.200 --> 00:12:16.960
Maybe Dany will convert to Kinvara’s Red
God, feeding her fire further, turning her

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:20.410
closer to violence and blood.

00:12:20.410 --> 00:12:24.150
Back beyond the Wall, Bran goes off and has
a vision without Bloodraven’s guidance,

00:12:24.150 --> 00:12:28.090
going back to the spot where he saw the white
walkers made, but much later.

00:12:28.090 --> 00:12:31.890
He sees the army of the dead, and he sees
the white walkers who lead them, including

00:12:31.890 --> 00:12:37.190
the Night King himself, who somehow touches
Bran, through the vision, leaving him marked,

00:12:37.190 --> 00:12:41.590
which breaks the magical protections on Bloodraven’s
cave, and leaves them all vulnerable to the

00:12:41.590 --> 00:12:42.590
walkers.

00:12:42.590 --> 00:12:45.700
Bran’s training under Bloodraven’s gotta
finish up real quick, so he plugs into the

00:12:45.700 --> 00:12:49.650
Matrix and starts downloading as much as he
can before they leave.

00:12:49.650 --> 00:12:51.790
Back at Castle Black, Jon and Sansa and co.

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:55.060
strategize, trying to work out which northern
houses might support them.

00:12:55.060 --> 00:12:57.290
The Boltons already have the Umbers and the
Karstarks.

00:12:57.290 --> 00:13:01.840
But they could still win the Manderleys, Glovers,
Mormonts, Cerwyns, Hornwoods, Tallharts, and

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:03.480
many other minor houses.

00:13:03.480 --> 00:13:07.640
If they can get the houses together, they
could stand a chance against the Boltons.

00:13:07.640 --> 00:13:11.370
Sansa also brings up the Tullys, who could
also be a huge help, but she lies to hide

00:13:11.370 --> 00:13:15.291
her meeting with Littlefinger, and his offer
of the knights of the Vale.

00:13:15.291 --> 00:13:19.500
It seems like Sansa doesn’t totally trust
Jon – or maybe she only lies to keep Littlefinger

00:13:19.500 --> 00:13:20.550
out of all this.

00:13:20.550 --> 00:13:24.380
Either way, she does give Jon a fancy new
coat so it seems like things aren’t too

00:13:24.380 --> 00:13:26.160
bad between them.

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:30.220
Everyone heads off to recruit allies, leaving
Edd in charge at Castle Black.

00:13:30.220 --> 00:13:35.290
Jon jokes about the Wall falling, which is
some seriously scary foreshadowing.

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:39.520
Then back beyond the Wall, Meera and Hodor
get packing, while Bran and Bloodraven keep

00:13:39.520 --> 00:13:42.280
greendreaming, but knock-knock, the walkers
are here.

00:13:42.280 --> 00:13:45.670
The children try to defend the cave with fire
grenades – but the walkers and wights get

00:13:45.670 --> 00:13:50.210
in Meera kills a walker, Summer’s killed
by wights, Bloodraven’s killed by the Night

00:13:50.210 --> 00:13:55.620
King, Leaf sacrifices herself, and Hodor has
a psychic warging time travel seizure vision

00:13:55.620 --> 00:13:59.740
of his own future death from the past while
he sacrifices himself, saving Bran and Meera

00:13:59.740 --> 00:14:04.760
by holding the door, and holy fuck, if that’s
not the biggest and bloodiest ten minutes

00:14:04.760 --> 00:14:07.310
in Game of Thrones since the Red Wedding.

00:14:07.310 --> 00:14:09.030
Let’s– process this.

00:14:09.030 --> 00:14:13.870
So Meera kills that white walker with spear
with head made of dragonglass – making her

00:14:13.870 --> 00:14:17.890
the third person known to kill a walker, along
with Sam and Jon, which is cool.

00:14:17.890 --> 00:14:20.430
The death of Summer is so sad.

00:14:20.430 --> 00:14:25.740
With Lady, Grey Wind, and Shaggydog all dead,
Ghost is the last known surviving direwolf.

00:14:25.740 --> 00:14:30.700
There is also Nymeria, who Arya let loose
in the riverlands in Season 1.

00:14:30.700 --> 00:14:35.240
There are strong hints in the books that she’s
still out there, leading a wolf pack – so

00:14:35.240 --> 00:14:41.350
we may see her again – but that’s just
two of the original six Stark direwolves left.

00:14:41.350 --> 00:14:45.400
The death of Bloodraven is huge, cause he’s
one of the oldest, most powerful and knowledgeable

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:49.800
and mysterious characters in the series, yet
we never really found out his secrets before

00:14:49.800 --> 00:14:51.020
he died.

00:14:51.020 --> 00:14:55.010
In the books we know he’s a hundred-year-old
Targaryen bastard and brother of the Watch.

00:14:55.010 --> 00:14:57.880
But beyond that, we really know nothing.

00:14:57.880 --> 00:14:58.880
Who is he?

00:14:58.880 --> 00:15:00.420
How did come to be a psychic tree?

00:15:00.420 --> 00:15:03.890
What does he know, what are his goals, and
what exactly was his plan for Bran?

00:15:03.890 --> 00:15:06.000
What’s his history with the walkers?

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:09.560
The way the Night King looked at him it looks
like they got years old beef.

00:15:09.560 --> 00:15:13.700
And Leaf – it is poetic that she was killed
by the monsters she created, but was she the

00:15:13.700 --> 00:15:15.650
last of her species?

00:15:15.650 --> 00:15:20.660
As far as we know, the children in that cave
were the last of the children of the forest.

00:15:20.660 --> 00:15:22.310
And finally – Hodor.

00:15:22.310 --> 00:15:25.670
Poor, sweet, innocent Hodor.

00:15:25.670 --> 00:15:30.460
We learn that Hodor is the way he is because
in a vision of the past, Bran warged into

00:15:30.460 --> 00:15:35.210
young Wylis, reached through his mind such
that his present self would hold the door

00:15:35.210 --> 00:15:38.060
to save Bran and Meera from wights.

00:15:38.060 --> 00:15:41.910
This is so tragic and fucked up on so many
levels.

00:15:41.910 --> 00:15:47.920
Wylis was a happy, healthy kid who had his
mind and his whole life taken away from him.

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:52.820
Every word he said for the rest of his life
was a premonition of his death, yet everyone

00:15:52.820 --> 00:15:55.180
around him just thought it was funny.

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:56.520
And did he have a choice in this?

00:15:56.520 --> 00:16:01.350
Did he know all his life the way he’d die,
and bravely continued on anyway?

00:16:01.350 --> 00:16:07.710
Or is he a handicapped man being taken advantage
of, used for reasons he didn't understand?

00:16:07.710 --> 00:16:14.060
Further, since Hodor was killed by wights,
he’ll probably be raised as a zombie himself,

00:16:14.060 --> 00:16:18.150
forced to serve even after his death.

00:16:18.150 --> 00:16:20.390
And this is all Bran’s fault.

00:16:20.390 --> 00:16:24.210
He messed up, having that vision on his own,
and as a result, most of his friends are dead,

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:28.900
and he destroyed the life of an innocent man,
past present and future.

00:16:28.900 --> 00:16:34.460
Bran’s learning the hard way that with great
power comes great responsibility.

00:16:34.460 --> 00:16:41.380
A lot people are asking about the whole time
travel thing, and it looks like this isn’t

00:16:41.380 --> 00:16:45.190
like Back to the Future, where Marty creates
alternate future timelines by changing the

00:16:45.190 --> 00:16:46.190
past.

00:16:46.190 --> 00:16:50.540
Bran didn’t change anything – he just
caused a past event which had already happened

00:16:50.540 --> 00:16:51.830
in his timeline.

00:16:51.830 --> 00:16:56.620
Hodor already was Hodor, Bran just went back
and made it happen, it’s time travel, but

00:16:56.620 --> 00:16:58.540
it's a closed loop, yeah?

00:16:58.540 --> 00:17:00.650
All in one fixed timeline.

00:17:00.650 --> 00:17:04.010
Like Bloodraven says, the past is written,
the ink is dry.

00:17:04.010 --> 00:17:08.379
So it's not like Bran can go to the past and
stop the walkers ever being made, or stop

00:17:08.379 --> 00:17:11.799
Ned from ever dying, the past is written.

00:17:11.799 --> 00:17:15.189
What Bran and Meera really need to worry about
is the future.

00:17:15.189 --> 00:17:18.010
Cause what are they gonna do now?

00:17:18.010 --> 00:17:21.240
They’re stuck in the middle of nowhere,
the wights and walkers are right behind them,

00:17:21.240 --> 00:17:25.749
they’ve got no Hodor to carry Bran, no Summer
to protect them, no Bloodraven to guide them.

00:17:25.749 --> 00:17:30.070
They’re gonna need to be rescued – and
their saviour will probably be this mysterious

00:17:30.070 --> 00:17:34.250
figure from the trailer, who might be Jon’s
long-lost uncle Benjen, who’s been missing

00:17:34.250 --> 00:17:36.620
beyond the Wall for like five seasons.

00:17:36.620 --> 00:17:41.539
It could also be Coldhands, a mysterious friendly
zombie from the books, or it maybe even some

00:17:41.539 --> 00:17:43.049
combination of the two?

00:17:43.049 --> 00:17:44.460
We’ll see what happens.

00:17:44.460 --> 00:17:47.629
Whoever rescues them, Bran and Meera will
probably head for the Wall.

00:17:47.629 --> 00:17:51.830
But if they do, will the Night King’s mark
on Bran be a problem?

00:17:51.830 --> 00:17:56.210
The Wall and Bloodraven’s cave both seem
to be protected by the same kind of magic,

00:17:56.210 --> 00:17:58.580
the magic of the children of the forest.

00:17:58.580 --> 00:18:02.880
What if the moment Bran steps through the
Wall, the whole thing comes crashing down,

00:18:02.880 --> 00:18:05.450
and the walkers walk right through?

00:18:05.450 --> 00:18:08.639
Poor Edd can’t catch a break.

00:18:08.639 --> 00:18:10.429
That was a hell of an episode.

00:18:10.429 --> 00:18:14.389
We're now half way through the season, and
with war in the north, Arya against the Faceless

00:18:14.389 --> 00:18:18.600
Men, red priests in Meereen, pirates sailing
east, and every possible fuckin crazy thing

00:18:18.600 --> 00:18:22.700
happening north of the Wall, not to mention
King’s Landing, and Oldtown, and Dorne,

00:18:22.700 --> 00:18:25.519
it's only gonna get more intense.

00:18:25.519 --> 00:18:26.519
Thank you for watching.

00:18:26.519 --> 00:18:30.500
These videos do take a lot of work to make
so if you’d like to support the channel,

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:34.269
and get behind-the-scenes updates, stuff like
that, please pledge on Patreon – there’s

00:18:34.269 --> 00:18:35.299
a link below.

00:18:35.299 --> 00:18:39.690
There’s also a link to art by Ertac Altinoz,
that’s his depiction of Euron there.

00:18:39.690 --> 00:18:43.879
But yeah thank you to all Patrons supporting
